<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Burgundian State</h1><p class="st-meta">1363 CE – 1482 CE · capital Dijon</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The patchwork realm of the Valois dukes of Burgundy, from Dijon to the North Sea, whose court set the fashion of 15th-century Europe.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1363 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-ii-of-france">John II of France</a> gave the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-burgundy">Duchy of Burgundy</a> to his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-bold">Philip the Bold</a>. Philip's marriage to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/margaret-iii-countess-of-flanders">Margaret of Male</a> brought <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-flanders">Flanders</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-artois">Artois</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/free-county-of-burgundy">Free County of Burgundy</a> in 1384. His grandson <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-the-good">Philip the Good</a> added <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-namur">Namur</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/duchy-of-brabant">Brabant</a>, Holland, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-zeeland">Zeeland</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/county-of-hainaut">Hainaut</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/county-of-luxembourg">Luxembourg</a> between 1421 and 1443.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The dukes held their lands by different titles under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and the Empire and tried to bind them with common institutions, a Chamber of Accounts, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/states-general-of-the-netherlands">States General</a> from 1464 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/order-of-the-golden-fleece">Order of the Golden Fleece</a>, founded in 1430. Flemish and Brabantine towns supplied wealth from cloth and trade, and painters such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jan-van-eyck">Jan van Eyck</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rogier-van-der-weyden">Rogier van der Weyden</a> worked for the court.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bold">Charles the Bold</a> sought a crown but was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nancy">Nancy</a> in 1477. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-xi">Louis XI</a> seized the duchy; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mary-of-burgundy">Mary of Burgundy</a> married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximilian-i-holy-roman-emperor">Maximilian of Austria</a>, and after her death in 1482 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-arras-1482">Treaty of Arras</a> split the inheritance, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a> passing to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/habsburg-netherlands">Habsburg Netherlands</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/burgundian-state.jpg" alt="Burgundian State" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: self-made Trasamundo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandera_de_Borgo%C3%B1a.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1363 CE – 1482 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Dijon</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Philip the Bold, Philip the Good, Charles the Bold</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>French and Middle Dutch</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a>, <a href="/countries/belgium">Belgium</a>, <a href="/countries/netherlands">Netherlands</a>, <a href="/countries/luxembourg">Luxembourg</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Valois Burgundy, Burgundian Netherlands, Burgundian Lands</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1422&amp;focus=burgundian-state" aria-label="Burgundian State on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="47